    "Description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: ipv4: raw: reject IP_HDRINCL packets with ihl \u003c 5 (CVE-2026-64114)\n\n* kernel: fuse: re-lock request before returning from fuse_ref_folio() (CVE-2026-64266)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: fib: free fib_alias with kfree_rcu() on insert error path (CVE-2026-64572)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: seq: close a re-opened queue timer in the destructor (CVE-2026-68202)\n\n* kernel: xfs: bounds-check buffer log item's dirty bitmap (CVE-2026-80536)\n\n* kernel: inet: frags: strip GSO state from fragments before reassembly (CVE-2026-80590)\n\n* kernel: vfio/pci: clear vdev-\u003emsi_perm after freeing it on init failure (CVE-2026-89777)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
